{
  "id": "FlinqLvMatch0001",
  "name": "flinq LV matching",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "c0ffee0000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -620,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 660,
        "content": "## How it works\n\nMatches positions from a GAEB tender against a product catalog, even when the wording differs. Downloads a sample X83 and a catalog CSV, parses the tender with flinq /v1/extract, then scores each position against the catalog with /v1/rerank. Output: one row per position with the best SKU and a score.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Create a free account at https://console.flinq.ai/signup\n2. Create an API key in the console\n3. Add a Header Auth credential \"flinq API\": name `Authorization`, value `Bearer flq_...`\n4. Assign it to \"Extract tender positions\" and \"Match position to catalog\"\n5. Run it\n\nOwn data: swap the two download URLs (GAEB .x81-.x86, catalog CSV with sku,name,description).\n\nPricing and current limits: https://flinq.ai/docs/pricing/\nPython version of the same pipeline: https://flinq.ai/docs/examples/lv-matching/"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c0ffee0000000002",
      "name": "Sticky Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        256,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "## 1. Load the catalog\n\nFetches the sample CSV and joins name + description into one match text per row. Keep the User-Agent header: the flinq.ai host rejects n8n's default agent with a 503."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c0ffee0000000003",
      "name": "Sticky Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        960,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "## 2. Parse the tender\n\nFetches the sample X83 and runs it through /v1/extract. The Code node flattens the group tree into one item per position (rno, qty, unit, text)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c0ffee0000000004",
      "name": "Sticky Note 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1664,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 430,
        "height": 400,
        "content": "## 3. Match positions\n\n/v1/rerank scores each position against all catalog texts. Calls are paced to stay inside the API's concurrency limit, see https://flinq.ai/docs/limits/ before raising the pace."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a1b2c3d4e5f60001",
      "name": "When clicking 'Execute workflow'",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "position": [
